# Git commits

- Work on a named branch (create one if needed before committing).
- Use conventional/semantic messages (`feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `refactor`, `style`, `docs`, `test`) with **one concern per commit**.
- **Never** add `Co-authored-by` trailers (including Cursor or any agent).
- **Never** pass `--trailer` with co-author metadata.
- Commit with message only (`-m` / `-F`). If the environment injects a Co-authored-by trailer, rewrite the commit with `git commit-tree` (via the real `git.exe`) so the final history has **no** co-author trailers.
- Do not leave injected trailer text inside the commit body either.
